\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Sensitivity of the selector on FMNIST at $N=30$. Panels (a) and (b) sweep the Dirichlet concentration $\alpha $ at $K=5$ and report final accuracy and the participation Gini coefficient. Panels (c) and (d) sweep the cohort size $K$ over three seeds and report the same two quantities. The strip below each panel gives the margin of the proposed selector over uniform random selection, signed so that upward always favours the proposed selector. Shaded bands are one standard deviation over seeds.}}{10}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:sweeps}{{2}{10}{\rev {Sensitivity of the selector on FMNIST at $N=30$. Panels (a) and (b) sweep the Dirichlet concentration $\alpha $ at $K=5$ and report final accuracy and the participation Gini coefficient. Panels (c) and (d) sweep the cohort size $K$ over three seeds and report the same two quantities. The strip below each panel gives the margin of the proposed selector over uniform random selection, signed so that upward always favours the proposed selector. Shaded bands are one standard deviation over seeds.}}{figure.2}{}}
